{"id": "EUVD-2026-103550", "enisaUuid": "156f95cc-6125-3911-af78-8e56b6c0d18b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsquashfs: Add dictionary size range check to prevent shift-out-of-bounds\n\nWhen an abnormal SquashFS image (COMP_OPTS flag is 1 but dictionary size\nis 0) is mounted, and performs shift operations using dictionarysize, the\nshift exponent is -1, causing a shift-out-of-bounds.\n\nDetail as below:\nsquashfs_comp_opts(msblk, buffer, length)\n  squashfs_xz_comp_opts()\n    if (comp_opts)\n      n = ffs(opts->dict_size) - 1;<----opts->dict_size=0, n=-1\n      if (opts->dict_size != (1 << n) && opts->dict_size !=\n\t  \t(1 << n) + (1 << (n + 1))) <----shift-out-of-bounds\n\nFix it by adding a dictionary size range check before the shift operation.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:20:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b02948a23455f8190a53887b2d2c13ae1d360cea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d9c5c218ea356a1d88765214ad2919605280ab1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a1c293e7aa17f1afaee0684e0e931fe23a5a6b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c68e0068a236f9a7dfc19720bdf11e5d80a85089", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88c673a0bd233df44ca0020da82f4fd3876de27a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0cb85377daaefb4ce5ce72975f2deb27ee0e0cad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e1ca4e3a380ef3e8f46ce006f1146392e3f32c98", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f7745fb3580152ca902ef181b605f33cabfb1d0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98636", "GHSA-wgfg-84p9-xmpv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00380bdf-0d6c-312a-b44d-5057ec09b9a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "03de17cc-524d-3bc2-bf29-6dde4f98a91c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff750311d30acc9564ef577050794953eee59f01 <88c673a0bd233df44ca0020da82f4fd3876de27a"}, {"id": "2349f7a1-defd-3bc4-addb-fe7e9cb58e21", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff750311d30acc9564ef577050794953eee59f01 <b02948a23455f8190a53887b2d2c13ae1d360cea"}, {"id": "39cfc2eb-d3b9-32f7-a64a-f7ff33d5f129", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "4d04e65e-acdc-378c-bb01-3d875f44f747", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff750311d30acc9564ef577050794953eee59f01 <c68e0068a236f9a7dfc19720bdf11e5d80a85089"}, {"id": "51b720ee-7dfe-313e-bd40-3a75b45026d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff750311d30acc9564ef577050794953eee59f01 <1f7745fb3580152ca902ef181b605f33cabfb1d0"}, {"id": "641a38d0-3954-3be6-8fd0-73793d26188c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "7224b3d3-445c-3679-b6cb-73f257254d33", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7dcc706d-b622-33af-8bb0-7a9a6e4e9ef3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "86e6e7ce-47eb-3128-a540-dd9b697b6848", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff750311d30acc9564ef577050794953eee59f01 <0cb85377daaefb4ce5ce72975f2deb27ee0e0cad"}, {"id": "9a90b6d4-0005-3749-aa0c-d4c3b1882736", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.39"}, {"id": "a316eb82-6ffd-364c-96dc-14ecaec7a7d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a8031bbe-78fd-3e8b-a398-e25926fae2d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "b81871e8-4906-3df9-8135-58c8a401d2e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "d2d328